137 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 84 0 R
/E (Prolonged toleration can entrench a structural limbo. Where toleration becomes the default solution for individuals with a pending or unenforceable return, it risks producing long-term uncertainty. This situation limits access to services, inhibits integration planning, and constrains participation in socio-economic life. The German case shows how toleration, although granting a lawful stay, can still deprive individuals of a tangible integration perspective when renewal is uncertain, and rights remain restricted. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
